The runner temporarily clears the SIGHUP-only privileged_extensions setting
through ALTER SYSTEM and reload, waits for fresh connections to observe it,
runs the unmodified init-script loop as the still-superuser postgres, then
resets the override and verifies the original setting before demotion/migrations.
These operations affect only the fresh disposable PGDATA tmpfs.
No extension is dropped, reassigned or altered in a hosted database.
